      "spam": false,
      "value": "Why would there even be a certificate there? Shouldn't the certificate be called from the issuing server every time?\nI found this weird and searched for google certificates using the method your posted. I have no certificates issued to google on my computer at all.\n\nAlso the only place where music did not work properly for me was the void club; It took an enourmous time for it to start. But that seemed to be a problem with the world itself; I am also pretty sure they fixed that.\n\nFor me youtube does not even use a google certificate. It uses a certificate from geotrust.\nSo I guess the problem you guys are having is that it tries to use a certificate issued to google even though youtube AND google don't use a certificate that is issued to \"google\" anymore?\n\nFor reference here is someone with that issue on youtube-dl github: https://github.com/rg3/youtube-dl/issues/11573#issuecomment-269896421",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
